# Avoid Custom Implementations

## Core Principle: Plugin-First Development

**Before writing any custom code, check if a plugin or dependency already provides the functionality.**

## Common Anti-Patterns to Avoid

### ❌ Custom Authentication
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom authentication
class CustomAuthService {
  generateToken(payload) {
    // Custom JWT implementation
  }
  
  verifyToken(token) {
    // Custom token verification
  }
}

// ✅ DO use jsonwebtoken
import jwt from 'jsonwebtoken';
const token = jwt.sign(payload, secret, { expiresIn: '24h' });
const decoded = jwt.verify(token, secret);
```

### ❌ Custom Password Hashing
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom password hashing
const hashPassword = (password) => {
  // Custom hashing logic
};

// ✅ DO use bcrypt
import bcrypt from 'bcrypt';
const hashedPassword = await bcrypt.hash(password, 10);
const isValid = await bcrypt.compare(password, hashedPassword);
```

### ❌ Custom State Management
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create complex state management
const [state, dispatch] = useReducer(complexReducer, initialState);
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
const [error, setError] = useState(null);

// ✅ DO use TanStack Query
const { data, isLoading, error } = useQuery({
  queryKey: ['data'],
  queryFn: fetchData
});
```

### ❌ Custom WebSocket Implementation
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom WebSocket handling
const socket = new WebSocket('ws://localhost:3000');
socket.onopen = () => { /* custom logic */ };
socket.onmessage = (event) => { /* custom logic */ };

// ✅ DO use Socket.io
import websocketService from '../services/websocketService.js';
websocketService.connect();
websocketService.subscribe('data', handleUpdate);
```

### ❌ Custom Form Handling
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom form management
const [formData, setFormData] = useState({});
const [errors, setErrors] = useState({});
const [touched, setTouched] = useState({});

// ✅ DO use React Hook Form
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
const { register, handleSubmit, formState: { errors } } = useForm();
```

### ❌ Custom Validation
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom validation
const validateEmail = (email) => {
  const regex = /^[^\s@]+@[^\s@]+\.[^\s@]+$/;
  return regex.test(email);
};

// ✅ DO use Zod
import { z } from 'zod';
const emailSchema = z.string().email();
const result = emailSchema.safeParse(email);
```

### ❌ Custom HTTP Client
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom HTTP client
class CustomHttpClient {
  async get(url) {
    // Custom fetch implementation
  }
  
  async post(url, data) {
    // Custom POST implementation
  }
}

// ✅ DO use fetch or axios
const response = await fetch(url);
const data = await response.json();
```

### ❌ Custom Logging
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom logging
const customLogger = {
  info: (message) => console.log(message),
  error: (message) => console.error(message)
};

// ✅ DO use Winston
import winston from 'winston';
const logger = winston.createLogger({
  level: 'info',
  format: winston.format.json(),
  transports: [new winston.transports.Console()]
});
```

### ❌ Custom CORS Handling
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom CORS middleware
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Origin', '*');
  res.header('Access-Control-Allow-Methods', 'GET,PUT,POST,DELETE');
  // Custom CORS logic
});

// ✅ DO use cors middleware
import cors from 'cors';
app.use(cors());
```

### ❌ Custom Security Headers
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom security headers
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  res.setHeader('X-Content-Type-Options', 'nosniff');
  res.setHeader('X-Frame-Options', 'DENY');
  // Custom security headers
});

// ✅ DO use helmet
import helmet from 'helmet';
app.use(helmet());
```

### ❌ Custom Compression
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom compression
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  // Custom compression logic
});

// ✅ DO use compression middleware
import compression from 'compression';
app.use(compression());
```

### ❌ Custom Request Logging
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom request logging
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  console.log(`${req.method} ${req.url}`);
  next();
});

// ✅ DO use morgan
import morgan from 'morgan';
app.use(morgan('combined'));
```

### ❌ Custom Cookie Parsing
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom cookie parsing
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  req.cookies = parseCookies(req.headers.cookie);
  next();
});

// ✅ DO use cookie-parser
import cookieParser from 'cookie-parser';
app.use(cookieParser());
```

### ❌ Custom Rate Limiting
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom rate limiting
const rateLimitMap = new Map();
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  // Custom rate limiting logic
});

// ✅ DO use express-rate-limit
import rateLimit from 'express-rate-limit';
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 100 // limit each IP to 100 requests per windowMs
});
app.use(limiter);
```

### ❌ Custom XSS Protection
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom XSS protection
const sanitizeInput = (input) => {
  // Custom XSS protection logic
};

// ✅ DO use xss library
import xss from 'xss';
const cleanInput = xss(userInput);
```

### ❌ Custom Database Connection Pooling
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom connection pooling
class CustomConnectionPool {
  constructor() {
    this.connections = [];
    this.maxConnections = 10;
  }
}

// ✅ DO use pg Pool
import { Pool } from 'pg';
const pool = new Pool({
  host: process.env.DB_HOST,
  port: process.env.DB_PORT,
  database: process.env.DB_NAME,
  user: process.env.DB_USER,
  password: process.env.DB_PASSWORD,
  max: 20
});
```

### ❌ Custom Error Handling
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom error handling
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Custom error handling logic
});

// ✅ DO use established error handling patterns
import { sendErrorResponse } from '../routes/optimizedRoutes.js';
```

### ❌ Custom Testing Framework
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom testing
class CustomTestRunner {
  describe(name, fn) { /* custom logic */ }
  it(name, fn) { /* custom logic */ }
}

// ✅ DO use Vitest
import { describe, it, expect } from 'vitest';
```

### ❌ Custom Build Tooling
```javascript
// ❌ DON'T create custom build tools
const customBuildTool = new CustomBuildTool();

// ✅ DO use Vite
import { defineConfig } from 'vite';
export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [react()]
});
```

## Plugin Discovery Process

### 1. Check package.json First
```bash
# Check what's already installed
cat package.json | grep -A 50 "dependencies"
```

### 2. Search for Existing Solutions
```bash
# Search for specific functionality
npm search "authentication"
npm search "validation"
npm search "logging"
```

### 3. Check Documentation
- **Express.js middleware** - Check Express.js documentation
- **React ecosystem** - Check React documentation
- **Node.js modules** - Check Node.js built-in modules

### 4. Use Established Patterns
```javascript
// ✅ USE established patterns from the codebase
import { executeCrudOperation } from '../routes/optimizedRoutes.js';
import websocketService from '../services/websocketService.js';
import { useParticipants } from '../hooks/useParticipants.js';
```

## When Custom Code is Appropriate

### ✅ Business Logic
```javascript
// ✅ APPROPRIATE - Domain-specific business logic
const calculateParticipantScore = (scores) => {
  return scores.reduce((sum, score) => sum + score, 0) / scores.length;
};
```

### ✅ Helper Functions
```javascript
// ✅ APPROPRIATE - Project-specific utilities
import { generateSlug, generateUniqueSlug } from '../utils/slugUtils.js';
import { normalizeInstagram } from '../routes/optimizedRoutes.js';
```

### ✅ Service Wrappers
```javascript
// ✅ APPROPRIATE - Simplified interfaces to complex plugins
import websocketService from '../services/websocketService.js';
import databaseService from '../services/databaseService.js';
```

### ✅ Component Logic
```javascript
// ✅ APPROPRIATE - React component-specific behavior
const ParticipantCard = ({ participant, onSelect }) => {
  const [isExpanded, setIsExpanded] = useState(false);
  
  return (
    <div onClick={() => onSelect(participant)}>
      {/* Component logic */}
    </div>
  );
};
```

## Plugin Integration Checklist

### Before Writing Custom Code
- [ ] Check package.json for existing dependencies
- [ ] Search npm for relevant packages
- [ ] Check if functionality exists in established patterns
- [ ] Verify if helper functions already exist
- [ ] Consider if it's truly project-specific logic

### After Choosing a Plugin
- [ ] Read plugin documentation
- [ ] Configure plugin properly
- [ ] Use plugin's recommended patterns
- [ ] Test plugin integration
- [ ] Document plugin usage

## Remember: Custom code should be the exception, not the rule. Always prefer established, tested, and maintained solutions.